url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-03-26T21:08:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-26T21:08:56Z","body":"I've capped it down to 30 fps and it still happens without PI enabled (with tickrate at 30 fps)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2755752642/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985861008","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104622#issuecomment-2985861008","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104622","id":2985861008,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6x-J-Q","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-18T22:19:15Z","updated_at":"2025-06-18T22:55:10Z","body":"in 4.5 dev 5 this issue has become even worse it seems, now even with PI it's broken.\n\nI'll run further tests to pinpoint when PI broke\n\nWeird.. The MRP doesn't exhibit the issue with 4.5 dev 5 with PI, just my project.. Trying to figure out why that is..\n\nPinpointed the difference, in my project in 4.5 dev 5 I'm not just freeing Mesh Instances (those aren't causing any problems) but I'm freeing Particle Systems that are causing a problem even with PI enabled.\nAlso, I've noticed that when PI is disabled if there is a mismatch between FPS and Physics FPS (say 144FPS with 30hz physics tickrate) I'm getting the issue without freeing stuff in 4.5 dev 5.\n\nOK, just tested 4.1.4 (pre FSR2 and PI, so just TAA) and I have been able to reproduce it with FPS-Physics Tick Rate Mismatch and TAA, and resolved it by matching the two by caping FPS to Physics Tick Rate...\nSo this is a Long standing issue with TAA\n\nI've updated the Main Post to better reflect the new discoveries regarding the problem","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2985861008/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989286177","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104622#issuecomment-2989286177","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104622","id":2989286177,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6yLOMh","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-19T22:44:56Z","updated_at":"2025-06-19T22:45:22Z","body":"Some Further Updates:\n\nThis issue happens for every object in motion when motion is taking place at a slower pace then the frames are rendered, but doesn't happen with static objects.\nExample used to test that was setting Physics Process to 1 FPS, and locking the FPS to 5 FPS, with the camera being static.\nThe in motion Objects during those 5 frames act as follows:\n1 Take a Step (Look Correct)\n2 Get messed up by TAA\n3-5 TAA gradually stabilizes the result\n6 Take a Step (Look Correct with previous frame's TAA properly applied)\n7 Gets Messed up again\n8+ starts stabilizing, and repeating this cycle onwards\n\nI'm still not sure what could be causing this sort of behavior, and why it only affects objects that are moving...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2989286177/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3081262363","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/104622#issuecomment-3081262363","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104622","id":3081262363,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc63qFUb","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-16T21:59:38Z","updated_at":"2025-07-16T21:59:38Z","body":"My suspicions of motion vectors going crazy has been confirmed (didn't know you could show all the debug modes in a running project before)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/04f4e364-e98e-4e8e-a8dc-486f48ec5b46","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3081262363/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"h